From: BE-IIS <support@be-iis.eu>
Subject: [PATCH] media: imx708: handle reset GPIO acquisition errors

devm_gpiod_get_optional() can return an error pointer.  Stop probing and
propagate that error instead of passing the error pointer to
gpiod_set_value_cansleep() during power-on and power-off.

This also preserves -EPROBE_DEFER when the GPIO provider is not ready yet.

Signed-off-by: BE-IIS <support@be-iis.eu>
---
 drivers/media/i2c/imx708.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/i2c/imx708.c b/drivers/media/i2c/imx708.c
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/imx708.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/imx708.c
@@ -1947,6 +1947,12 @@ static int imx708_probe(struct i2c_client *client)
 	/* Request optional enable pin */
 	imx708->reset_gpio = devm_gpiod_get_optional(dev, "reset",
 						     GPIOD_OUT_HIGH);
+	if (IS_ERR(imx708->reset_gpio)) {
+		ret = PTR_ERR(imx708->reset_gpio);
+		dev_err_probe(dev, ret,
+			      "failed to acquire reset GPIO\n");
+		return ret;
+	}
 
 	/*
 	 * The sensor must be powered for imx708_identify_module()
-- 
